## Step 1: Push Code to GitHub

Your repository has already been initialized and committed with all necessary files (`Dockerfile`, `render.yaml`, `vercel.json`, and dynamic URL resolution).

Run the following command from your terminal to push it to your GitHub account:

```bash
git push -u origin main
```

*(If prompted, authenticate using your GitHub Personal Access Token or GitHub Desktop/browser).*

---

## Step 2: Set Up Free Cloud MySQL (Aiven or Railway)

### Option A: Aiven for MySQL (Recommended — Free Tier, No Expiring Trial)
1. Go to [aiven.io](https://aiven.io) and create a free account.
2. Click **Create Service** → select **MySQL** → pick the **Free** plan.
3. Once provisioned (approx. 2 minutes), go to **Service Overview**.
4. Note the following values:
   - **Host** (e.g. `mysql-xxxx.aivencloud.com`)
   - **Port** (e.g. `12345`)
   - **User** (`avnadmin`)
   - **Password** (shown in console)
   - **Database Name** (`defaultdb`)
5. Your JDBC URL format will be:
   ```
   jdbc:mysql://<HOST>:<PORT>/defaultdb?ssl-mode=REQUIRED
   ```

### Option B: Railway MySQL
1. Go to [railway.app](https://railway.app) and sign in with GitHub.
2. Click **New Project** → **Provision MySQL**.
3. Under the **Connect** tab, copy `DATABASE_URL`, `DB_USERNAME`, and `DB_PASSWORD`.

> [!NOTE]
> When the backend boots with the `prod` profile, Hibernate (`ddl-auto=update`) and `DataInitializer` will **automatically create all tables, seed default cryptocurrency assets, and provision the admin and demo user accounts** upon first startup.

